       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm it first because the dose looks like it could be an error.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose for adults is **800 mg**. This order is twice that.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for adults is **3,200 mg/day**. This order is twice that.\n\nAt this dose, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and other toxicity goes up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n1. **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total). This is a common analgesic dose, and \"1600\" may have been meant as the daily total.\n2. **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum prescription dose, usually for inflammatory conditions.\n3. **1600 mg PO four times daily** as written. If this is truly intended, please confirm and give the clinical reason. I'll add a note to the order saying the dose is above standard maximums and was confirmed by you.\n\nWhich do you want?"
      }
