       "text": "I entered the order as written: **ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth, four times daily (6,400 mg/day). Order ID: ORD-0001.**\n\nThe order includes a note saying the dose is above standard maximums, that you were told about this and confirmed it, and that no clinical reason was recorded. It also asks for pharmacist review, so pharmacy will probably contact you before dispensing.\n\nYou haven't given a clinical reason for this dose. If there is one, please add it to the chart to help pharmacy verify the order quickly. If this patient does stay on it, consider:\n- **Kidney function:** check creatinine and urine output often.\n- **Stomach protection:** a PPI, plus watching for signs of GI bleeding.\n- **Other risks:** blood pressure, fluid status, and drug interactions such as anticoagulants, ACE inhibitors or ARBs, and diuretics.\n\nIf you meant 400 mg or 800 mg per dose, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order. You would need to cancel ORD-0001 separately."
